            "review_text": "Discover06205185974\n1 contribution\n0\nLying about the actual price on the menu\nJun 2026 • Couples\nThe experience was very bad at the Ut Hong Bar, the price on the other menu, outside the other price. I call seafood rice, beefsteak potatoes, sponge tea, Ya-ua. The four items we see in the menu are as follows: 76k fried seafood rice, 71k beefsteak, 10k Ya-ua, 21k foam pink tea. So calculating each increase of 2k 3k, red tea, the restaurant opposite the newspaper 21k and calculated 22k. The problem is not how much the difference is, but transparency, space for lies, fraud. The menu does not change the price on the menu even though the menu already sees a new price. YOU SHOULDN’T GO TO THE RESTAURANT, YOU FOOL!! You will be charged differently than the actual price.\nRead more\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten June 6, 2026",
