            "review_title": "Review at Quan An UT HUONG",
            "review_text": "Diana N\n101 contributions\n0\nVietnamese Steak & Eggs for breakfast!\nMay 2016 • Friends\nUt Huong is another one of your hole on the wall establishments found in HCM.\n\nThey whip up many things in their kitchen, but my group and I came for their Bò né, Vietnamese steak & eggs. Now the Vietnamese steak & eggs is much different than the American steak & eggs. Don't expect a medium-well thick cut of meat and scrambled eggs. They give you a thin slab of beef with sunny side up eggs all still sizzling on a skillet. Be careful, the oil sizzling on the skillet tend to fly about and may burn you! The meal was very delicious; it is also accompanied with French bread where you can tear and dip in eggs & soy sauce which the Vietnamese love to do. By the way, each dish only cost us a $1 US!!!\n\nIf you happen to be by this place, it is definitely worth a try if you want a sizzling good time.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2017",
